<PageLayout title='About' {headings} info={{ slug: '/about-me', hideComment: true }}>
  <h2 id='who-am-i'>Profile</h2>
  <p>
    I am David Alonso (David7ce), a web developer by training. I completed a two-year degree in
    web application development and have taken additional courses. I speak Spanish and English,
    and this site is available in both.
  </p>
  <p>
    I build small web apps, command-line and desktop tools and websites, and I write notes about
    what I learn along the way.
  </p>

  <h2 id='interests'>Interests and Direction</h2>
  <p>My interests have grown beyond web development towards:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Systems and computer architecture</li>
    <li>Rust</li>
    <li>Linux and free and open-source software</li>
    <li>AI, developer tooling, APIs and integrations</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Outside of software I am interested in electronics, physics, technical investigation and
    teaching.
  </p>
  <p>
    These describe where my curiosity is heading. For what I have actually built, see the
    <a href='/en/projects'>projects</a>; for what I write while learning, see the
    <a href='/en/blog'>blog</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id='tools'>Technologies</h2>
  <p>Technologies I have used in my studies and projects. This is not a proficiency ranking.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Languages</strong>: Bash, C#, JavaScript / TypeScript, PHP; Rust and Python in some personal projects</li>
    <li><strong>Markup and styling</strong>: HTML, Markdown, XML, CSS</li>
    <li><strong>Databases</strong>: MariaDB, PostgreSQL, T-SQL</li>
    <li><strong>Web frameworks and CMS</strong>: ASP.NET, Angular, React, Astro, WordPress, Joomla</li>
    <li><strong>Environment</strong>: Arch Linux, Windows 11, VS Code, Git</li>
    <li><strong>AI coding assistants</strong>: Claude Code, GitHub Copilot</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The <a href='/en/stack'>Stack</a> page lists the tools I use in more detail.</p>

